      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Northern plains super forces commonly recruit external elders so demonic path Gu Immortals can become righteous and help Huang Jin tribes manage the region.",
      "chapters": [
        553
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_northern_plains",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "fac_huang_jin_bloodline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ye Lui tribe and Hei tribe are both called super forces, and both have Gu Immortals backing them. Their mortal tribe leaders share the same status on that footing.",
      "chapters": [
        604
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "gu-immortal-backing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_ye_lui_tribe",
        "fac_hei_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Jade Pool blessed land is named the headquarters of Huang Jin family’s Dong Fang tribe, a super force.",
      "chapters": [
        657
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "gu-immortal-backing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_jade_pool_blessed_land",
        "fac_dong_fang_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Dong Fang tribe could keep the name of a super force while declining to the point of having no real power, until a Gu Immortal rose and rebuilt it.",
      "chapters": [
        660
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
